262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Low-code platforms such as Zoho Creator simplify application development by providing forms, reports and workflows that can be assembled visually. Where specific requirements go beyond the standard components, pro-code extensions provide additional flexibility, and custom Deluge functions can introduce application-specific logic in a reusable form.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (In this experiment, a custom function named generateTicketQR was created with the Deluge language, the Default namespace, the string return type and two string arguments in the Event Registration application. The function was saved, listed in the Functions section and executed successfully, returning the expected confirmation message for the supplied attendee name. Although the function was simple, it illustrates the procedure for creating, executing and verifying a custom function. Combining low-code development with suitable pro-code extensions can support more flexible application development, in which standard functionality is built visually and specific logic is added through code where it is required.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
